1
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:10,750
A ridge tent is a triangular prism.

2
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,870
Its end is a triangle 2 metres wide and 1.5 metres high.

3
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:17,330
The tent is 3 metres long.

4
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,640
How much air is inside the tent, in cubic metres?

5
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:24,210
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:30,150
The triangle's area is a half times 2 times 1.5, which is 1.5 square metres.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:38,130
That triangle runs the whole 3 metres, so the volume is 1.5 times 3, which is 4.5 cubic metres.

8
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:43,230
Remember: the volume of a cuboid is length times width times height.

9
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:48,960
A 5 by 3 by 2 centimetre cuboid has a volume of 30 cubic centimetres.

10
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,780
A prism has the same cross-section all along its length.

11
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:57,560
Its volume is the area of the cross-section, times the length.

12
00:00:57,610 --> 00:00:59,130
A cuboid is a prism too.

13
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:04,980
For a triangular prism, the volume is a half, times b, times h, times the length.

14
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:05,680
Your turn.

15
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:10,740
A prism has a cross-section of 5 square metres and a length of 4 metres.

16
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:12,070
What is its volume?

17
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:15,370
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:17,720
5 times 4 is 20 cubic metres.

19
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:23,820
Volume is measured in cubic units, like cubic centimetres and cubic metres.

20
00:01:23,870 --> 00:01:27,540
And 1 litre is 1,000 cubic centimetres.

21
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,920
Here is the method.

22
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:33,660
Step 1: find the triangle's base and perpendicular height.

23
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:38,270
Step 2: the cross-section area is a half, times b, times h.

24
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:42,010
Step 3: multiply by the length of the prism.

25
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:45,500
Step 4: write the answer in cubic units.

26
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:50,830
A wedge has a triangular end with base 6 centimetres and height 4.

27
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,930
It is 15 centimetres long.

28
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:57,530
The cross-section is a half times 6 times 4, which is 12.

29
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:02,760
The volume is 12 times 15, which is 180 cubic centimetres.

30
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:03,500
Your turn.

31
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:07,780
A triangle with base 4 and height 3 makes a prism 10 long.

32
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:09,180
What is its volume?

33
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:12,210
Pause and work it out.

34
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,900
A half times 4 times 3 is 6.

35
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:17,090
6 times 10 is 60.

36
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:20,890
A prism has a volume of 210 cubic centimetres.

37
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:27,160
Its cross-section is a triangle with base 5 and height 6, so the area is 15.

38
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:32,410
The length is 210 divided by 15, which is 14 centimetres.

39
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:38,230
A triangular prism has a triangle with base 8 and height 5, and a length of 10.

40
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,780
Zoe finds the volume.

41
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:41,800
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:42,980
Line 1 is wrong.

43
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,460
She forgot the half.

44
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:51,220
The cross-section is a triangle, so its area is a half times 8 times 5, which is 20.

45
00:02:51,270 --> 00:02:54,490
20 times 10 is 200.

46
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:58,350
A water trough for animals is a triangular prism.

47
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:05,050
Its end has base 40 centimetres and height 30, and it is 150 centimetres long.

48
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:11,180
The volume is 600 times 150, which is 90,000 cubic centimetres.

49
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:16,110
Divide by 1,000: it holds 90 litres of water.

50
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,500
One last question.

51
00:03:17,550 --> 00:03:20,840
How many litres is 5,000 cubic centimetres?

52
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,330
Pause the video and answer.

53
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:28,060
1 litre is 1,000 cubic centimetres.

54
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:32,350
5,000 divided by 1,000 is 5 litres.

55
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:38,200
To remember: the volume of a prism is the cross-section area times the length.

56
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:41,790
A triangle cross-section has area a half b h.

57
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,820
Rearrange to find a missing length.

58
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:48,790
1 litre is 1,000 cubic centimetres.

59
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:54,230
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.3 on Camday.
